Rule 9
    - The normal Single Final Rules makes ties all be the lowest place (i.e. 
four way tie for 2nd place would result in four placed 2nd. With Multi-final rules
each of the ties needs to work like this: 
    If there are 6 dancers, and there is a 4 way tie for 2nd. then places are as follows:
    1st = 1,
    2nd - 5th place = ((5th - 2nd) / 2) + 2nd = 3.5,
    6th = 6

    The way you would fix this is by changing certain variables to floats in the 
Ruler.java class, but it breaks every other class if you change that, they didn't
think about this situation when the code was originally written. The code doesn't
use local variables, which makes it much more difficult. See the method 
"absoluteTie" in Ruler.java...

